problem:
Problem description
- A single-period cutting-stock planning problem is considered over a planning horizon $$\mathcal{T}$$.
- There is a set of product types $$\mathcal{P}$$, where each product type $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$ has a required cut length $$\ell_p$$ and a customer demand quantity $$d_p$$.
- Raw steel pipes are identical and each pipe has length $$L$$ and unit purchase value $$c^{\mathrm{pipe}}$$.
- Cutting patterns are used to describe how one raw pipe is cut into pieces of the product types. Each pattern is indexed by $$k \in \mathcal{K}$$.
- The number of distinct cutting patterns used in the plan may not exceed $$K^{\max}$$.
- For any chosen cutting pattern, the number of pieces cut from one raw pipe may not exceed $$M^{\max}$$.
- For any chosen cutting pattern, the unused leftover length of the raw pipe may not exceed $$W^{\max}$$.
- The selected cutting plan must satisfy all customer demands for every product type in $$\mathcal{P}$$.
- Each raw pipe is assigned to exactly one cutting pattern.
- The total cost combines the purchase cost of raw pipes and an additional surcharge that depends on how frequently each cutting pattern is used.
- The selected cutting patterns are ranked from most frequently used to least frequently used, and the surcharge applied to rank $$r$$ is governed by a multiplier $$\gamma_r$$.
- The optimization goal is to choose the cutting patterns and assign raw pipes to them so that the total cost is minimized while respecting all demand, pattern-count, piece-count, and leftover-length requirements.
- A solution is represented by:
  - The set of selected cutting patterns, with at most $$K^{\max}$$ distinct patterns.
  - For each selected pattern $$k$$, a recipe indicating how many pieces of each product type $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$ are cut from one raw pipe.
  - For each selected pattern, the number of raw pipes assigned to that pattern.
  - The usage rank of each selected pattern, ordered by frequency of use.
  - The total cost of the entire cutting plan.

Input Format
{
  "planning_horizon": {
    "type": "singleton set",
    "meaning": "Single-period horizon $$\\mathcal{T}$$"
  },
  "number_of_product_types": {
    "type": "integer",
    "meaning": "$$P = |\\mathcal{P}|$$"
  },
  "raw_pipe_length": {
    "type": "scalar",
    "meaning": "Length of one raw pipe, $$L$$"
  },
  "item_lengths": {
    "type": "array",
    "shape": "length $$P$$",
    "meaning": "Required length of product type $$p$$, denoted by $$\\ell_p$$ for each $$p \\in \\mathcal{P}$$"
  },
  "demands": {
    "type": "array",
    "shape": "length $$P$$",
    "meaning": "Demand quantity of product type $$p$$, denoted by $$d_p$$ for each $$p \\in \\mathcal{P}$$"
  },
  "unit_raw_pipe_value": {
    "type": "scalar",
    "meaning": "Unit value or purchase cost of one raw pipe, $$c^{\\mathrm{pipe}}$$"
  },
  "max_distinct_patterns": {
    "type": "integer",
    "meaning": "Maximum number of distinct cutting patterns allowed, $$K^{\\max}$$"
  },
  "max_pieces_per_pipe": {
    "type": "integer",
    "meaning": "Maximum number of pieces allowed from one raw pipe under any pattern, $$M^{\\max}$$"
  },
  "max_leftover_length": {
    "type": "scalar",
    "meaning": "Maximum allowed leftover length for any pattern, $$W^{\\max}$$"
  },
  "rank_based_surcharge_multipliers": {
    "type": "array",
    "shape": "length $$K^{\\max}$$",
    "meaning": "Rank-based surcharge multipliers $$\\gamma_r$$ for pattern rank $$r$$, ordered from most frequently used to least frequently used"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "selected_patterns": {
    "type": "array",
    "shape": "up to $$K^{\\max}$$ entries",
    "meaning": "List of selected cutting patterns"
  },
  "pattern_details": {
    "type": "array",
    "shape": "one record per selected pattern",
    "meaning": {
      "pattern_id": "Identifier of the selected pattern",
      "recipe": "Array of length $$P$$ giving the number of pieces of each product type cut from one raw pipe under this pattern",
      "pipes_assigned": "Number of raw pipes assigned to this pattern",
      "usage_rank": "Rank of the pattern among selected patterns, with $$1$$ being the most frequently used",
      "rank_multiplier": "Surcharge multiplier associated with the usage rank"
    }
  },
  "total_cost": {
    "type": "scalar",
    "meaning": "Minimized total cost of raw pipes plus pattern-frequency surcharges"
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "planning_horizon": [1],
  "number_of_product_types": 4,
  "raw_pipe_length": 1850,
  "item_lengths": [290, 315, 350, 455],
  "demands": [15, 28, 21, 30],
  "max_distinct_patterns": 4,
  "max_pieces_per_pipe": 5,
  "max_leftover_length": 100,
  "unit_raw_pipe_value": 1,
  "rank_based_surcharge_multipliers": [0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4]
}
